The numbers from 1 to 100 that are divisible by 2 are those of the form \(2k\) for \(k = 1,2,\dots,50\), giving \(50\) numbers. Among these, the numbers that are also divisible by 3 are exactly those divisible by \(\operatorname{lcm}(2,3)=6\). The count of numbers divisible by 6 is \(\left\lfloor\frac{100}{6}\right\rfloor = 16\). Therefore, the numbers divisible by 2 but not by 3 is \(50 - 16 = 34\).

The probability is \(\frac{34}{100} = \frac{17}{50}\).

